# swap-of-three-numbers
 This Python program demonstrates how to swap the values of three numbers. It takes three numbers as input from the user, displays their original values, and then swaps them using Python’s multiple assignment feature. This program helps beginners understand variables, user input, and value swapping in Python.
# Swap three numbers

a = int(input("Enter first number: "))
b = int(input("Enter second number: "))
c = int(input("Enter third number: "))

print("Before swapping:")
print("a =", a)
print("b =", b)
print("c =", c)

# Swapping
a, b, c = c, a, b

print("After swapping:")
print("a =", a)
print("b =", b)
print("c =", c)
